Problem with python 3 syntax when building stack from scratch on hydra
PR: #813
@cekees

This is to report what I believe are two bugs in the computational Kernel related to 3D Hessians. 

**Bug 1**
In this line: https://github.com/erdc/proteus/blob/master/proteus/CompKernel.h#L1077, instead of `[I*2+J] = 0.0;`, I think it should be `[I*NSPACE+J] = 0.0;`. Note that this is not a specialized function (to 2D problems) but one general for NSPACE. 

**Bug 2**
I think the function in this line: https://github.com/erdc/proteus/blob/master/proteus/CompKernel.h#L1111 is wrong. The function should init hess_trial to zero before doing certain computations. This is partially done; i.e., some entries are not zero out. Currently, the first loop is: 

```
    for (int j=0;j<NDOF_TRIAL_ELEMENT;j++)
      for(int I=0;I<NSPACE;I++)
	hess_trial[j*NSPACE+I] = 0.0;
```

I think it should be: 

```
    for (int j=0;j<NDOF_TRIAL_ELEMENT;j++)
      for(int I=0;I<NSPACE;I++)
        for(int J=0;J<NSPACE;J++)
          hess_trial[j*NSPACE2+I*NSPACE+J] = 0.0;
```

